/-!
# Complete non-involution coverage in the actual star Sylow

Every one of the 1024 stabilizer-chain entries either squares to the identity
or is conjugate to a fixed representative from `Data`. All identities use the
literal permutations, and all 24 points are checked. These certificates need
no normality assumption and supply no classification of arbitrary radicals.

Source tables: the ATLAS max1 words in `QuotientInvolutions.SylowData` and
the certified Sylow stabilizer chain. `source/generate.py` discovers witnesses;
the finite equalities here are independently checked by the Lean kernel.
-/
@[expose] public section
